+; RUN: opt -passes='print<access-info>' -memory-check-merge-threshold=10000 -disable-output %s 2>&1 | FileCheck %s
+
+; These 8 loads model a fully unrolled inner loop. Ranges here differ
+; only by constant offsets and should form 1 group checked against `%out`.
+; Using only the greedy algorithm exhausted a merge threshold of 2 and emitted
+; 5 checks instead of 1. The constant offset lookup however will keep merging
+; these accesses regardless of the greedy comparison budget since its cheap.
